/* net session: connect to a real Phonalyser server, then disconnect.

   The address is not known when this script is written - the server binds port
   0 so the OS picks a free one - so it arrives through param(), which is the
   one sanctioned bridge from the engine into a sandboxed body (a body may not
   name System).

   'var' is a reserved word rather than a type name, and String is java.lang,
   so both pass the sandbox scan; the compile-only tests in ScriptCompilerTest
   pin that, so this scenario cannot be broken by a tightened rule without
   something else going red first.

   The failure REASON is recorded rather than collapsed into a boolean: a run
   that reports only "connected: false" tells nobody whether the port was
   wrong, the handshake was refused, or no server was there at all. */
var error = netConnect(param("server", ""));
if (error != null) {
    failCheck("connect", error);
}
waitUntil("the session to come up", () -> netIsConnected(), 5);
checkTrue("connected", netIsConnected());

netDisconnect();
waitUntil("the session to close", () -> !netIsConnected(), 5);
checkTrue("disconnected", !netIsConnected());
